FRCSoftware's learning course uses Commands v3 which does not run on a RoboRIO.
However, Commands v2 does. 
This additional resource is similar to Stage 1B where it walks you through how to program the 2026 kitbot using the Commands v2 framework.
Commands v2 is outside of the learning course's scope and it will **not** be used outside of this additional resource. 

<Aside type="note">
    Please note, the code was only
    tested in a simulation. It was not tested on a real kitbot. Code may not
    function as expected.
</Aside>

## Key Concepts

Commands define individual robot actions (deploy the intake, index a game piece, drive based on joystick inputs).
Triggers define when commands should run (controller input, sensor data reaches a certain threshold, the start of autonomous or teleop).
Subsystems represent the physical robot mechanisms that commands require and control (intake, indexer, drivetrain).

